<h1>DSL (Dice Specific Language)</h1>
<ul>
<li><code>&lt;count&gt;&lt;type&gt;</code> designates <code>count</code> dice of <code>type</code><ul>
<li><code>&lt;count&gt;</code> is a number</li>
<li>normal numerical dice are written as <code>d6</code> (6-sided dice, faces valued at 1 to 6).</li>
<li>fate dice are designated <code>f</code></li>
<li>if no type is given, count is taken to be a flat modifier (perhaps negative)</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>aggregate modes<ul>
<li>sum <code>+</code> adds the values together</li>
<li>advantage <code>^</code> takes the highest value of any die</li>
<li>count <code>#/&lt;target&gt;</code> or <code>#\&lt;target&gt;</code> counts the dice that roll over or under target</li>
<li>target <code>/&lt;target&gt;</code> or <code>\&lt;target&gt;</code> successful if the previous</li>
<li>examples<ul>
<li><code>+ /15</code> - add dice together. Success is greater or equal to 15</li>
<li><code>#\3 /4</code> - count the number of dice that rolled under 3, looking for at least 4</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>concatenate, as in for d66 tables</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>names <code>&lt;name&gt; =</code> gives a name</li>
<li>unknown <code>?</code> designates a number which should be left as an input box</li>
</ul>
<h1>aggregates</h1>
<p><code>+</code> sum (default)
<code>#</code> count of faces (pool)
<code>= &gt; &lt; &gt;= &lt;= !=</code> target</p>
<h1>operators</h1>
<p><code>+</code> add
<code>^</code> <code>!^</code> advantage/disadvantage
<code>name</code> name</p>
<ul>
<li>exploding dice</li>
</ul>
<h1>values</h1>
<p><code>f</code> fate/fudge dice
<code>d</code> numerical dice
<code>p</code> pips
<code>%</code> previous dice set</p>
<h1>Rolling with Advantage</h1>
<p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X_DdGRjtwAo">numberphile video</a></p>
<p>probability for any number x in 2dN^ <code>p(x) = (2x-1)/N**2</code>
average for 2dN^ <code>(N+1)*(4N-1)/(6N)</code> ~2/3
average for 3dN^ ~&gt;3/4</p>
